<title>AUSTRIA: BUBA'S WELTEKE SEES NO NEED FOR GERMAN REPO CHANGE.</title>
<headline>BUBA'S WELTEKE SEES NO NEED FOR GERMAN REPO CHANGE.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Wednesday he saw no need for a change in Germany's repo rate.</p>
<p>&quot;For the time being I see no need to act,&quot; he said in response to reporters' questions on whether the Bundesbank planned to adjust the rate.</p>
<p>&quot;We should continue to keep our course so as not to unsettle the markets,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Welteke added he was confident that the planned single European currency would start on time.</p>
<p>&quot;I continue to believe that EMU will start on January 1, 1999,&quot; he told reporters during a conference organised by the Austrian National Bank.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom 43-1 531 12 254</p>
